    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53076" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάνης</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ητος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a mat of reeds</i> such as the Athen. women took with
			them when they went out, Lex Solonis ap.<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sol.</u>
				21
			</span></i>: generally, <i>mat</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.23
			</span></i> (pl.): prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ κ. τῆς κοίτης
				ὑπερέχει</span>, of those who make a show abroad with
			poverty at home, <i><span class="en">
				Crates Com.
				12
			</span></i>, cf. Phot.s.v.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίκνον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				6.86
			</span></i>.</div>
